        <mxCell id="class-note" value="&lt;b&gt;Modeling notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;code&gt;app.py&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;auth_service.py&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;repository.py&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;database.py&lt;/code&gt; are Python modules, not declared Python classes; they are shown as UML module components with their real functions.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;code&gt;Result&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Config&lt;/code&gt; are actual classes. &lt;code&gt;DuplicateUsernameError&lt;/code&gt; is an actual exception class.&lt;br&gt;• The project returns SQLite &lt;code&gt;sqlite3.Row&lt;/code&gt; records; &lt;code&gt;users&lt;/code&gt; is the real SQL table, not a Python ORM model." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff7e6;strokeColor=#d69e36;fontColor=#704d12;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
